From bef40e1996051b34351bec7f8f717f72bd80f727 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thiago Duarte <me@tduarte.co>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:07:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: softisp: awb: Add white point locus clamp and zone
 gating

Port of the fp6-img libcamera 0.7.2 AWB patches to the 0.8.0 softisp IPA,
where AWB moved to libipa:

  ipa: simple: awb: Add optional white point locus clamp and damping
  ipa: simple: awb: Gate the gray-world estimate on near-neutral zones
  (Jorijn van der Graaf)

The locus and the per-zone statistics are as in the originals. What is
different: the locus is read from libipa's existing colourGains key (the
feature is enabled by the presence of clampMargin), the clamped target is
handed to libipa's grey-world implementation as synthetic means so its
smoothing and controls keep working, and the damping / fast-converge logic
is dropped in favour of libipa's own smoothing. Zone sums follow 0.8.0's
statistics and leave saturated pixels out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
